  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 18, ‘Relative proportions of (a) medical doctors and (b) nursing personnel aged over 55 years and below 35 years, by income group’ (Source: WHO National Health Workforce Accounts, 2025, latest available data over 2015–2024). Two scatter plots — panel (a) for medical doctors and panel (b) for nursing personnel — plotting each country’s percentage aged <35 on the horizontal axis (0% to 80%) against its percentage aged 55+ on the vertical axis (0% to 60%), colour-coded by World Bank FY 2026 income group (Low-income, Lower-middle-income, Upper-middle-income, and High-income countries), with a diagonal equality line indicating where the share of workers near retirement (55+) equals the share of young workers (<35).",
